# Security

- Never commit secrets (`.env`, tokens, keys, credentials). Never log secrets.
- Validate all external input at API boundaries (path/query/body). Prefer typed parsing (e.g. serde + validators).
- Use parameterized SQL via SQLx — no string-built queries.
- Authn/authz on protected routes; do not trust client-only checks.
- Escape/encode for XSS on any user-controlled HTML; prefer text nodes / safe frameworks.
- Error responses must not leak internals (stack traces, DB details) to clients.
- For expense/money paths: treat amounts and ownership as sensitive; authorize by user.
- Before shipping auth or money changes, load `.cursor/skills/security-review/SKILL.md`.
